most all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 32424, "best_position": 19}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": 30536, "best_position": 23}, {"artist": "The Weeknd", "streams": 23220, "best_position": 67}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": 22711, "best_position": 13}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 21119, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": 16095, "best_position": 29}, {"artist": "Maroon 5", "streams": 15629, "best_position": 32}, {"artist": "The Chainsmokers", "streams": 11154, "best_position": 80}, {"artist": "Cigarettes After Sex", "streams": 10604, "best_position": 87}, {"artist": "PinkPantheress", "streams": 10246, "best_position": 99}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "sg", "country_name": "Singapore", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": 64660, "best_position": 2}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 32424, "best_position": 19}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": 23930, "best_position": 11}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": 22711, "best_position": 13}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 21119, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": 16095, "best_position": 29}, {"artist": "Maroon 5", "streams": 15629, "best_position": 32}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": 14914, "best_position": 41}, {"artist": "The Chainsmokers", "streams": 11154, "best_position": 80}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "folk": {"genre": "folk", "country_code": "sg", "country_name": "Singapore", "summary": "Folk music can have a number of different meanings, including:\n\nTraditional music: The original meaning of the term \"folk music\" was synonymous with the term \"Traditional music\", also often including Roots music; the term \"Traditional music\" was given its more specific meaning to distinguish it from the other definitions that \"Folk music\" is now considered to encompass.\nFolk music can also describe a particular kind of popular music which is based on traditional music.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Olivia Rodrigo", "streams": 98592, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Shawn Mendes", "streams": 16636, "best_position": 27}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": 14914, "best_position": 41}, {"artist": "One Direction", "streams": 11693, "best_position": 75}, {"artist": "Clairo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ed Sheeran", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ellie Goulding", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gracie Abrams", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lorde", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Phoebe Bridgers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "sg", "country_name": "Singapore", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 35211, "best_position": 12}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 32424, "best_position": 19}, {"artist": "Post Malone", "streams": 10788, "best_position": 86}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Toliver", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Frank Ocean", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Halsey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "IVE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Joji", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "jazz": {"genre": "jazz", "country_code": "sg", "country_name": "Singapore", "summary": "Jazz is a musical art form which originated around the beginning of the 20th century in Black communities in the Southern United States from a confluence of African and European music traditions. The style's West African pedigree is evident in its use of blue notes, call-and-response, improvisation, polyrhythms, syncopation, and the swung note of ragtime.\n\nFrom its early development until the present, jazz has also incorporated music from 19th and 20th century American popular music, which is based on European music traditions.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 21119, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Steve Lacy", "streams": 16814, "best_position": 25}, {"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Laufey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "sg", "country_name": "Singapore", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 32424, "best_position": 19}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": 30536, "best_position": 23}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": 25100, "best_position": 56}, {"artist": "ENHYPEN", "streams": 14951, "best_position": 40}, {"artist": "CORTIS", "streams": 13497, "best_position": 52}, {"artist": "Hearts2Hearts", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "IVE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jennie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KiiiKiii", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NMIXX", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "sg", "country_name": "Singapore", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Olivia Rodrigo", "streams": 98592, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": 71565, "bes